Using a muonic dataset equivalent to 3.0 inverse femtobarns collected by the LHCb experiment, an assessment of the form of the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate was conducted. Initial results from this analysis do not provide conclusive evidence to favor either the vector meson dominance model or CW model over other theoretical approaches, as indicated by parameters best-fit values of $\sigma_{1}=0.56^{+0.18}_{-0.16}$ and $\sigma_{2}=1.06^{+0.20}_{-0.18}$. Furthermore, estimates for rare decay processes $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ and $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ were derived, yielding values of $0.37^{+0.15}_{-0.13}$ and $1.13^{+0.48}_{-0.43}$ per $10^{-8}$ respectively.

